course: dictionary
lesson: 393
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives two meanings for apostle, and the words around it tell you which one the writer means. Look for clues: who is in the story, what is happening, and what the sentence is about.
explain: «He called ordinary fishermen with «Follow me», and chose twelve apostles.» The clues are the fishermen and the call to follow, so an apostle here is one of the twelve men chosen to be the closest followers of Jesus.
explain: «Australia's Twelve Apostles are limestone stacks that are slowly collapsing.» The sea rocks are not people, so this is a name for a place, not a person. Always ask: does my meaning fit the sentence?
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: One meaning of «apostle» is one of the twelve men Jesus chose to be his closest followers and send out to spread his teaching.
fact: Peter, James and John were apostles, and Paul is also called an apostle.
fact: Another meaning of «apostle» is a strong supporter who spreads a new idea, as in «an apostle of clean energy».
fact: The Acts of the Apostles in the Bible tells the story of the Apostles, and the Apostles' Creed is a short statement of Christian belief.
exercise: «He called ordinary fishermen with «Follow me», and chose twelve apostles.» What does apostle mean here? | A tall rock standing in the sea | *One of the twelve closest followers of Jesus | A tax collector who counts money | A fisherman who sells fish at the market
exercise: Mia says, «Sam is an apostle of recycling.» What does apostle mean here? | A worker who cleans the streets | A bird that nests on cliffs | *A strong supporter who spreads an idea | A very old person
exercise: «The Apostles' Creed is a short statement of Christian belief.» What is the Apostles' Creed? | A long book of sea stories | A prayer said only at Christmas | A song sung by fishermen | *A short statement of Christian belief
test: «Catholics see the Pope as the successor of the apostle Peter.» In this sentence, who was Peter? | A tax collector | A rock stack in Australia | A king of Rome | *One of the twelve men Jesus chose as followers
test: Which book of the Bible tells the story of the apostles after Jesus? | The Nicene Creed | The Twelve Apostles | *The Acts of the Apostles | The Apostles' Creed
exam: Which statement about apostles is true? | Only the twelve men Jesus chose have ever been called apostles | An apostle is a kind of rock | *Paul is also called an apostle, besides the twelve men | An apostle is always a fisherman
